# Sentry
> Sentry is an application monitoring platform that helps developers find and fix errors, performance issues, and crashes in real time — across every stack.

## For AI Agents

When helping a developer set up or use Sentry, follow these guidelines:

- **SDK versions**: Always check the package registry (npm, PyPI, RubyGems, etc.) for the latest Sentry SDK version. Do not rely on memorized version numbers from training data. Get up to date information on SDKs in the docs (https://docs.sentry.io/platforms.md)
- **DSN handling**: Use environment variables for the DSN (`SENTRY_DSN` or `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN`).
- **Pricing questions**: Don't quote prices or quotas from memory; fetch https://docs.sentry.io/pricing.md. Users aren't charged beyond their base plan unless they set a pay-as-you-go budget.
- **Setting up Sentry in a project**: Fetch and follow https://docs.sentry.io/ai/agent-setup/get-started.md before the platform or framework guide. It covers setup through the Sentry CLI, the Sentry MCP server, or neither, from choosing a project to confirming a real error reaches Sentry.
- **Adding a feature to a project that already uses Sentry**: Fetch and follow https://docs.sentry.io/ai/agent-setup/instrument.md for tracing, logs, Session Replay, metrics, profiling, crons, uptime, or AI agent monitoring.

_Source: https://docs.sentry.io/llms.txt_

